# Allowlist: ignore everything, then un-ignore what we track.
# Reference clones (refs/), ROMs, extracted assets and build output never get committed.
*
!*/
!.gitignore
!.gitmodules
!README.md
!dev.sh
!scripts/
!scripts/*.sh
!tools/
!tools/*.py
!tools/*.sh
!tools/*.c
!docker/
!docker/Dockerfile
!docker/qemu-plugin.h
# the Miyoo Mini release: game.json, the launch templates, the packer, its README
!README_MIYOO.md
!miyoo/
!miyoo/*.json
!miyoo/templates/
!miyoo/templates/*
!miyoo/tools/
!miyoo/tools/*.py
# the launcher icon, our own drawing (miyoo/icon.svg -> miyoo/icon.png; the PNG is allowed again below *.png)
!miyoo/icon.svg
# The port itself: subtree of inspectredc/fzerox + our port changes.
# game/.gitignore (the decomp's own) keeps ROM-derived output out; the lines
# at the bottom repeat the important ones as a second fence.
!game/
!game/**
# Never, even if allowlisted above:
refs/
*.z64
*.n64
*.v64
*.ndd
*.o2r
*.otr
# Second fence for the game tree (ROM-derived output, build products, tools).
game/baserom*
game/asm/
game/bin/
game/build/
game/src/assets/
game/include/assets/
game/.splat/
game/.venv/
game/tools/ido-recomp/
game/linker_scripts/*/*/auto/
game/linker_scripts/*/*/*.ld
game/*.yaml
!game/decomp.yaml
!game/config.yml
game/torch.hash.yml
*.mio0
*.bin
*.o2r
*.ppm
*.png
# ...except the drawn launcher icon (ours, not from the ROM)
!/miyoo/icon.png
# the Miyoo64 repository's docs
!SETTINGS.md
